          "value": "",
          "version": 1
        },
        "output_image_geometry_path": {
          "value": "Selected Patterns",
          "version": 1
        },
        "parameters_version": 1
      },
      "comments": "Copy the adjacent acquisition-grid cells (67,10) and (68,10), inclusive, with every cell array and pattern kept in the same order. Preserve the full scalar map for context; no resampling, feature renumbering, or detector-pixel crop.",
      "filter": {
        "name": "nx::core::CropImageGeometryFilter",
        "uuid": "e6476737-4aa7-48ba-a702-3dfab82c96e2"
      },
      "isDisabled": false
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "removed_data_path": {
          "value": [
            "OIM Nickel/Cell Data/Pattern",
            "OIM Nickel/Cell Data/X Position",
            "OIM Nickel/Cell Data/Y Position",
            "Selected Patterns/Cell Data/X Position",
            "Selected Patterns/Cell Data/Y Position"
          ],
          "version": 1
        },
        "parameters_version": 1
      },
      "comments": "After copying the selected patterns, remove the full-map Pattern array (101109600 bytes) and both geometries' unpopulated X Position/Y Position arrays. This reader creates those coordinate arrays but leaves zeros for this input, so retain source scan IDs and geometry origin/spacing instead. Original HDF5 and import peak memory are unchanged.",
      "filter": {
        "name": "nx::core::DeleteDataFilter",
        "uuid": "bf286740-e987-49fe-a7c8-6e566e3a0606"
      },
      "isDisabled": false
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "endian_index": {
          "value": 0,
          "version": 1
        },
        "output_path": {
          "value": "Data/Output/OIM_Nickel_Pattern_Examples/Inspection",
          "version": 1
        },
        "file_extension": {
          "value": ".bin",
          "version": 1
        },
        "input_data_array_paths": {
          "value": [
            "Selected Patterns/Cell Data/Pattern"
          ],
          "version": 1
        },
        "parameters_version": 1
      },
      "comments": "Write Pattern.bin: two consecutive 60 by 60 uint8 detector images, pattern then row then column, 7200 bytes with no header. Endianness has no effect on one-byte uint8. This is not an EDAX UP1 file.",
      "filter": {
        "name": "nx::core::WriteBinaryDataFilter",
        "uuid": "06912cbc-9745-4098-8d44-c674974d2ca8"
      },
      "isDisabled": false
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "output_style_index": {
          "value": 1,
          "version": 1
        },
